	"townhall-beds-hint": "Each settler needs a bed. Wanderers only come while there is a free bed, so build beds to grow the colony.",
	"townhall-jobs": "Jobs",
	"townhall-jobs-hint": "Jobs show settlers / places. Orange means a hut has a free place. Couriers and jobless settlers need no hut.",
	"townhall-roles-hint": "Members can use the colony's things. Officers can also give jobs, order buildings and welcome wanderers. Only the owner sets roles and Permadeath.",
	"townhall-wanderers": "Wanderers",
	"townhall-wanderers-hint": "Wanderers wait at the Town Hall. Welcome them or turn them away on the Citizens tab. A Tavern brings them sooner and lets you hire recruits.",
	"guide-townhall": "The Town Hall is the heart of the colony. Its land protects everything around it, and its window has these tabs:<br><br><strong>Actions</strong>: the colony's name (the pencil renames it), its numbers, and the Town Hall's own upgrade.<br><strong>Quests</strong>: how far the colony's shared quests are, with a button that opens the quest book (also on the L key).<br><strong>Town map</strong>: the colony from above, with the edge of its land, every building and the settlers. Scroll the mouse wheel or use + and − to zoom, drag with the mouse to move around, and point at a building to see its name.<br><strong>Banners</strong>: the colony banner (from Heraldry: Banners), and buttons that copy it onto the banners of the Town Hall, the Guard Towers or every building.<br><strong>Information</strong>: a log of what happened in the colony, and every work order waiting for a builder.<br><strong>Citizens</strong>: Current Citizens, every living settler with their food and bed, and Dead Citizens, who died and whether they have been buried. Officers pick each settler's job here, Recall stuck ones and answer wanderers.<br><strong>Statistics</strong>: settlers against beds, how many workers each job has, and what the huts have done.<br><strong>Permissions</strong>: the players in the colony and their roles.<br><strong>Settings</strong>: Permadeath, wanderers and the warehouse.",
