	"residence-nowhere": "There is no free bed anywhere else for this settler and their family.",
	"residence-empty": "Nobody lives here yet. Settlers move in when they need a bed and there is a free one here.",
	"residence-hint": "Settlers sleep in the building they live in. Couples either have beds next to each other or share one; children sleep near them. Children are only born if the colony has a free bed. Residents without a job look after the farmland in the building using tools and resources from a chest in the house or the warehouse.",
	"residence-household": "The {0} household",
	"residence-single": "{0} (on their own)",
	"guide-residence": "<strong>Residence</strong><br>Where families live, like MineColonies' houses. Every settler who sleeps in a bed inside the building is one of its residents.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the Residence, order upgrades, and open its storage (the hut block).<br><strong>Residents</strong>: each household living here (a couple and their children, or someone on their own), their jobs, children's time to grow up, and whether a couple can have a child right now.<br><br>Two single adults who have lived in the colony for a couple of days pair up and move in together. A couple who are not hungry may have a child when the colony has a free bed. Children grow up into settlers who can be given a job.",
