	"family-cmd-nochild": "{0} is not a child.",
	"family-cmd-bad-couple": "Those two can't be a couple (one is a child, a visitor, already in a couple, or they are related).",
	"job-prospector": "Prospector",
	"job-miner": "Miner",
	"job-quarrier": "Quarrier",
	"block-hut-prospector": "Prospector's Hut",
	"block-hut-miner": "Miner's Hut",
	"block-hut-quarry": "Quarry",
	"block-waypoint-mine": "Mine waypoint",
	"block-waypoint-quarry": "Quarry waypoint",
	"blockdesc-waypoint-mine": "For blueprints. Put it in a Miner's Hut blueprint on the ground where the middle of the mine shaft starts. The builder skips it.",
	"blockdesc-waypoint-quarry": "For blueprints. Put it in a Quarry blueprint on the ground in the middle of where the pit goes. The builder skips it.",
	"building-prospector": "Prospector's Hut",
	"building-miner": "Miner's Hut",
	"building-quarry": "Quarry",
	"wand-tab-mining": "Mining",
	"wand-tab-note-mining": "The Prospector finds ore, the Miner digs a mineshaft and the ore the Prospector found, and the Quarry digs a stone pit.",
	"hut-placed-prospector": "{0} placed. Put a prospecting pick in its storage (sneak + right-click), then give a settler the Prospector job.",
	"hut-placed-miner": "{0} placed. Put a pickaxe in its storage and give a settler the Miner job. The miner digs a mineshaft beside the hut, and also digs ore a Prospector finds.",
	"hut-placed-quarry": "{0} placed. Put a pickaxe in its storage and give a settler the Quarrier job. The quarrier digs a stone pit beside the Quarry.",
	"hint-prospector": "Up to two prospectors work here. In Manage workers, set each to Finds ore (needs a prospecting pick) or Mines ore (needs a pickaxe and torches). Finders take readings within {0} blocks (see the Work area tab) and search more where ore looks good. Readings show on the Ore tab, the Town Hall and your world map. Miners dig out the best ore found.",
	"hint-miner": "Put a pickaxe in the hut's storage, plus a shovel and torches if you have them. The miner builds a mineshaft: an entrance from the surface, then one level under another, with tunnels it picks itself off every level, digging any ore it sees. A level 0 hut has level 1, each upgrade adds a level, and at the top hut level it goes as deep as it can. Planks and logs are needed for the supports. When the mine is done or waiting for materials, and Go to prospected ore is on (Ore tab), it digs ore a Prospector found within {0} blocks.",
	"hint-quarry": "Put a pickaxe in the hut's storage, plus a shovel if you have one. The quarrier digs a square pit beside the Quarry, one layer at a time, with stairs round the edge, and breaks out whole rock blocks. Upgrade the Quarry for a wider, deeper pit.",
	"guide-prospector": "<strong>Prospector's Hut</strong><br>The prospector looks for ore with the game's prospecting pick.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a prospecting pick in the storage.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far out the prospector goes, and whether a guard goes along.<br><strong>Ore</strong>: every ore found so far, the best reading of each and where it was.<br><br>The prospector walks 25 to 50 blocks between readings, anywhere in its work area, and wears the pick down a little each time. Like a player following the pick, it heads where the readings around look best: near red (very poor) readings it rarely looks again, near yellow and green ones it looks much more. Every colony member sees the readings on the Colony prospecting layer of their world map, kept apart from their own readings.",
	"guide-miner": "<strong>Miner's Hut</strong><br>The miner digs a mine beside the hut, and goes to dig ore a Prospector found.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a pickaxe in the storage.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far from the hut the miner may go for prospected ore, and whether a guard goes along.<br><strong>Ore</strong>: turn Go to prospected ore on or off, and see the ores the colony's prospectors found. Press Mine this to go for one ore only, Any ore to let the miner pick the best reading, or New mine to start a fresh staircase there.<br><strong>Levels</strong>: each loop of the mineshaft's stairs. Mine here sends new tunnels to a level first; Repair puts a level back the way it was.<br><strong>Settings</strong>: the fill block for holes in the floor, and how deep the mine may go.<br><strong>Guards</strong>: guards from Guard Towers on Patrol mine who go with the miner.<br><strong>Required resources</strong>: what the mineshaft piece being dug still needs. The ^ button puts what you carry into the hut.<br><strong>Minimum stock</strong> and <strong>Statistics</strong>: as on every hut.<br><br>The shaft is a spiral staircase round a pillar of rock, so the miner can walk down and back up with what it dug. Every turn of the spiral is a level, 8 blocks deeper, with a tunnel straight out from each side. Each hut level allows two more levels. The miner digs out any ore it sees on the way. It never digs next to water or lava, into a building or into someone else's land. Bring torches if you go down to look: the mine is dark.",
	"guide-quarry": "<strong>Quarry</strong><br>The quarrier digs a pit right beside the Quarry for whole rock blocks.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the Quarry, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a pickaxe in the storage.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: whether a guard goes along.<br><strong>Quarry</strong>: where the pit is and how big it is.<br><br>The quarrier picks a side of the Quarry facing away from the Town Hall, first clears what stands above the ground there, then digs the pit a layer at a time. A staircase is left round the edge, each block one step lower than the one before. Inside the staircase every other block of rock is left standing, in a checkerboard that also changes from layer to layer, so once the blocks round it are dug it stands free on all six sides. The quarrier then breaks it out whole: the game's relieving. At level 1 the pit is 5 by 5 blocks and 6 deep; each upgrade makes it 2 blocks wider and 6 deeper.",
	"workarea-range-hint-prospector": "The prospector takes readings in this range, 25 to 50 blocks apart, and spends more time where they look good.",
	"workarea-range-hint-miner": "The miner only goes to readings within this range of the hut.",
