	"tool-hammer": "hammer",
	"workstatus-needs-tool-hammer": "needs a hammer (put one in the hut storage or the warehouse)",
	"hut-placed-smelter": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1 (it has a fire pit), give a settler the Smelter job, and put nuggets, charcoal, a fired crucible and fired ingot molds in its storage.",
	"hut-placed-blacksmith": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1 (it has a forge), put an anvil next to it, give a settler the Blacksmith job, and put a hammer, ingots, charcoal and sticks in its storage.",
	"hint-smelter": "Put nuggets, charcoal, a fired crucible and fired ingot molds in the hut's storage (couriers bring them too). The smelter melts the nuggets on the fire pit and pours ingots. Copper needs charcoal or coal, not firewood. The Smelting tab sets how many ingots to keep.",
	"hint-blacksmith": "Put a hammer, ingots, charcoal and sticks in the hut's storage (couriers bring them too). The blacksmith needs a forge and an anvil within 8 blocks of the hut, good enough for the metal. The Smithing tab sets how many of each thing to keep.",
	"guide-smelter": "<strong>Smelter's Hut</strong><br>The smelter melts nuggets into ingots with the game's fire pit, crucible and ingot molds.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put nuggets, charcoal, a fired crucible and fired ingot molds in the storage.<br><strong>Smelting</strong>: every metal the game melts in a crucible, how many ingots the colony has, and how many to keep. The smelter only works on metals you keep some of.<br><br>The smelter keeps up to 4 molds set out beside the fire pit and melts up to 4 ingots at a time, one kind of nugget per crucible (no bronze yet). Copper melts at about 1084 degrees, so it needs charcoal or coal; tin and lead melt with firewood.",
	"guide-blacksmith": "<strong>Blacksmith's Hut</strong><br>The blacksmith makes tool heads, tools and other metal pieces from ingots, with the game's forge and anvil. Once you build an Armourer's Hut or a Weaponsmith's Hut, armor parts or weapons are made there instead.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a hammer, ingots, charcoal and sticks in the storage.<br><strong>Smithing</strong>: everything the game's smithing recipes make from the metals the colony has ingots of, with how many ingots each takes. Set how many to keep; the blacksmith only makes what you keep some of.<br><br>The blacksmith does not move voxels one by one like you do: it strikes the anvil a number of times that grows with the size of the piece, and its Smithing skill makes the work faster. A tool head is put on a stick, so the colony gets the finished tool. Place an anvil within 8 blocks of the hut; a copper anvil works copper, bronze anvils work bronze, and so on.",
	"tab-smelting": "Smelting",
	"smelting-hint": "The smelter makes ingots until the colony has this many of each metal, counting the warehouse, this hut and the molds. The second number is nuggets per ingot.",
