	"hut-placed-sawmill": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, give a settler the Sawyer job, and put a saw and logs in its storage (sneak + right-click).",
	"hint-sawmill": "Put a saw and logs in the hut's storage (couriers bring logs too). The sawyer makes planks and other things made only from wood, like support beams and sticks. The Sawmill tab sets how many of each to keep.",
	"guide-sawmill": "<strong>Sawmill</strong><br>The sawyer saws logs into planks and makes other wooden things, with a saw.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a saw and logs in the storage.<br><strong>Sawmill</strong>: everything the game's crafting recipes make from wood alone that the colony has the wood for, with how many pieces of wood each takes. Set how many to keep; the sawyer only makes what you keep some of. A new Sawmill keeps 16 planks of each wood.<br><br>The sawyer works at the hut block itself, one recipe at a time, and its Carpentry skill makes the work faster. What it makes goes to the warehouse.",
