	"hut-placed-mineshaftentrance": "{0} placed. The outline shows where its mine entrance goes. Link Miner's Huts to it, and their miners dig it.",
	"guide-mineshaftentrance": "<strong>Mineshaft Entrance</strong><br>Its building is the mine entrance itself: the outline shows it around the block. The linked Miner's Huts' miners dig and build it, not a builder. Several Miner's Huts can work the one mine.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: the Miner's Huts working this mine and their miners. Link adds a hut, Unlink takes it off.<br><strong>Levels</strong> and <strong>Settings</strong>: the same as on the Miner's Hut. They change the mine for every linked hut.<br><br>Put down near a Miner's Hut's mine, it takes that mine over. Put down near a derelict mine, it takes that one on. A new Miner's Hut near it joins it by itself. The deepest the mine goes is set by the highest level linked hut.",
