	"collect-hint-hunter": "The animals the hunter may hunt. Turn one off to leave it alone.",
	"job-craftsman": "Craftsman",
	"block-hut-craftsman": "Primitive Craftsman",
	"building-craftsman": "Primitive Craftsman",
	"hut-placed-craftsman": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, give a settler the Craftsman job, and put flint and sticks in its storage (sneak + right-click).",
	"hint-craftsman": "The craftsman knaps flint and stones into tool heads and puts them on sticks. Couriers bring flint, stones and sticks from the warehouse. Finished tools go to the warehouse, where other workers pick them up. The Knapping tab sets how many of each to keep.",
	"guide-craftsman": "<strong>Primitive Craftsman</strong><br>The craftsman makes stone tools for the colony.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Knapping</strong>: how many of each tool to keep. Only stones the colony has are shown.<br><br>Put flint or knappable stones and sticks in the warehouse or the hut storage. The craftsman knaps a head, then puts it on a stick. Finished tools go to the warehouse, and workers take the tools they need from there.",
	"tab-knapping": "Knapping",
	"knapping-hint": "The craftsman makes things until the colony has this many, counting the warehouse and this hut. The second number is how many stones and sticks one takes.",
	"knapping-none": "Nothing to show yet: put some flint or stones in the warehouse or this hut's storage.",
