	"hut-placed-tailor": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, give a settler the Tailor job, and put a knife and twine in its storage (sneak + right-click).",
	"hut-placed-jeweller": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, give a settler the Jeweller job, and put a hammer in its storage (sneak + right-click).",
	"hint-tailor": "The tailor mends worn clothes and leather or linen armor, but never metal armor. Set clothes to make on the Crafting recipes tab. It needs a knife; couriers bring twine, cloth and leather.",
	"hint-jeweller": "The jeweller makes the jewellery set on the Crafting recipes tab, from metal bits, chains and gems. It needs a hammer. Settlers take jewellery from the warehouse to wear, which makes them happier.",
	"guide-tailor": "<strong>Tailor's Hut</strong><br>The tailor makes and mends clothes.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a knife in the storage.<br><strong>Crafting recipes</strong>: the clothes and leather or linen armor to keep in the colony.<br><strong>Priorities</strong>: mending comes first unless you move something above it.<br><br>Settlers in rags leave their old clothes in the warehouse. The tailor fetches them and mends them with twine, cloth or a sewing kit, and armor with linen or leather. It never mends metal armor. With Tailor's Delight installed it also uses that mod's needles, awls, threads and buttons.",
	"guide-jeweller": "<strong>Jeweller's Workshop</strong><br>The jeweller makes necklaces, bracelets, brooches and pins.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a hammer in the storage.<br><strong>Crafting recipes</strong>: the jewellery to keep in the colony.<br><br>It works with metal bits, chains and gems. Settlers take jewellery from the warehouse to wear, and each piece (up to two) makes them happier. You can craft these pieces yourself too.",
