	"hut-placed-armourer": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, put a forge and an anvil next to it, give a settler the Armourer job, and put a hammer, ingots and charcoal in its storage.",
	"hut-placed-weaponsmith": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, put a forge and an anvil next to it, give a settler the Weaponsmith job, and put a hammer, ingots, charcoal and sticks in its storage.",
	"hint-armourer": "The armourer smiths chains, scales and plates, puts metal armor together (Crafting recipes tab) and mends worn metal armor. It needs a forge and an anvil within 8 blocks.",
	"hint-weaponsmith": "The weaponsmith smiths swords, spears, maces, blades and arrowheads. It needs a forge and an anvil within 8 blocks. The Smithing tab sets how many to keep.",
	"guide-armourer": "<strong>Armourer's Hut</strong><br>The armourer makes and mends metal armor.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a hammer, ingots and charcoal in the storage.<br><strong>Smithing</strong>: chains, scales, plates and lamellae to keep.<br><strong>Crafting recipes</strong>: the metal armor to keep, put together from those parts.<br><br>It fetches worn metal armor from its hut and the warehouse and mends it at the anvil with one more part of the same metal. Guards leave worn armor in the warehouse when a better piece is there. Leather and linen armor is the Tailor's.",
	"guide-weaponsmith": "<strong>Weaponsmith's Hut</strong><br>The weaponsmith makes weapons from ingots, with the game's forge and anvil.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades. Put a hammer, ingots, charcoal and sticks in the storage.<br><strong>Smithing</strong>: the swords, spears, maces, shields, blades and arrowheads to keep.<br><br>Once you build it, the Blacksmith stops making weapons and its weapon list moves here.",
